    values:originalText "(2) Where a source agency receives particular information under Step 1, 4 or 6 of a data matching cycle, the agency must destroy that particular information within 90 days of its receipt unless, within those days:  (a) the agency has considered that particular information and made a decision:  (i) to take action allowed by subsection (1) on the basis of that particular information; or  (ii) to carry out an investigation of the need to take action allowed by subsection (1) on the basis of that particular information; or  (b) the agency has, by using sampling procedures, identified that particular information as information that will form the basis for the agency:  (i) to take action allowed by subsection (1) on the basis of that particular information; or  (ii) to carry out an investigation of the need to take action allowed by subsection (1) on the basis of that particular information." ;
