concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-12-2-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12(5) Rules relating to privacy"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-12-2-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) After the 3-year period ending on 30 June 1998, and after each successive 3-year period, each agency must give the Minister responsible for the agency a report for presentation to the Parliament including all the details relating to the data-matching program carried out during the period that are specified for the purposes of this subsection in rules issued under this section. Note: Section 34C of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 sets time limits for giving reports to Ministers and for presentation of reports to the Parliament.   Data-matching  Part 2  Section 13  Data-matching Program (Assistance and Tax) Act 1990  Compilation date: 01/07/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(5) After the 3-year period ending on 30 June 1998, and after each successive 3-year period, each agency must give the Minister responsible for the agency a report for presentation to the Parliament including all the details relating to the data-matching program carried out during the period that are specified for the purposes of this subsection in rules issued under this section. Note: Section 34C of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 sets time limits for giving reports to Ministers and for presentation of reports to the Parliament.   Data-matching  Part 2  Section 13  Data-matching Program (Assistance and Tax) Act 1990  Compilation date: 01/07/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ce2e69a6156481439fecabc5ddaacf87f963ee0e854f3c45fa07efa2d1fb7967" ;
    values:partOf concept:data-matching-program-assistance-and-tax-act-1990-sec-12-2 ;
